---
/**
 * The audience section. Third stop, between the problem and the proof video:
 * the reader has just been told their pain, and the next question is whether
 * this thing is aimed at someone like them. It has to be answered before the
 * proof, not after, or the video plays to a reader who is not sure it is
 * theirs.
 *
 * NO PERSONA GRID. The competitors segment by customer type because they sell
 * to restaurants, groups, ghost kitchens and hotels. CostCook sells to one
 * kind of kitchen. Inventing four personas to fill a row of cards is the exact
 * move that makes a page read like a marketing department, which is the thing
 * this reader arrived braced for.
 *
 * THE MISFIT LIST IS THE POINT. For someone who came in from a cold email,
 * being told plainly what this is not for buys more trust than any list of who
 * it is for, and it is the one thing a page selling to them will not do.
 * Every line is already documented and cannot be softened here (RC-44):
 *
 *   several locations  ->  /compare "Several locations", a no row
 *   lot tracking       ->  /compare "Lot tracking and FSMA 204", a no row
 *   permission grid    ->  /compare "Tiered user access", a no row
 *   the restaurant     ->  RC-01 for the audience and RC-03 for the mechanism:
 *                          the estimate starts from a costed menu plus a guest
 *                          count, which is not the shape a fixed daily service
 *                          has. It is a fit statement, NOT a capability claim,
 *                          and it may not be written as one.
 *
 * If any of those four ever changes, the /compare row moves first and this
 * list follows it. No CTA here on purpose: the reader is deciding whether to
 * keep reading, not whether to buy.
 */
import { spellCapital } from '../../lib/words';
import SectionHandoff from '../SectionHandoff.astro';

const notFor = [
	{
		title: 'You run one restaurant on a fixed daily menu',
		body: 'Everything here starts from an event with a guest count. A service that repeats daily is a different shape, and a tool built for it will fit you better.'
	},
	{
		title: 'You need several locations to see their own shelves',
		body: 'CostCook is one kitchen workspace. There is no per-site inventory and no roll-up across sites.'
	},
	{
		title: 'You need lot tracking for FSMA 204',
		body: 'This was built for caterers, not for a facility under a traceability rule.'
	},
	{
		title: 'You need a permission grid for a big team',
		body: 'Owner and manager roles gate setup. Beyond that there is no per-screen control, so you cannot hand over the prep list and keep someone out of the costs.'
	}
];
---

<!-- story: docs/stories/homepage-visual-guidance.story.md -->
<!-- TWO COLUMNS SINCE 2026-08-29. The fit statement stays on the left; the
     misfit list moves into the right column as one ticket, so the section is a
     single frame (who it is for, beside who it is not for) instead of a text
     column over a text grid with the right 40% of the viewport empty. The
     four lines are unchanged and still bound by RC-44. -->
<section id="who" class="container-page py-section-tight" aria-labelledby="who-heading">
	<div class="grid gap-12 lg:grid-cols-[6fr_5fr] lg:gap-16">
	<div class="max-w-3xl" data-reveal>
		<p class="eyebrow">Who this is for</p>
		<h2 id="who-heading" class="mt-4 text-h2 font-semibold">
			Built for the kitchen where the person who quotes the job also cooks it.
		</h2>
		<p class="mt-5 max-w-[66ch] text-lede text-ink-soft">
			Catering and meal prep, run by an owner-operator with a small crew. You price jobs
			that change, you buy for dates rather than a steady week, and nobody down the hall
			owns the spreadsheet. That is the whole audience.
		</p>
		<h3 class="mt-10 text-h3 font-semibold">And plainly, who it is not for.</h3>
		<p class="mt-4 max-w-[66ch] text-ink-soft">
			{spellCapital(notFor.length)} kitchens should
			<a href="/compare" class="btn-quiet">buy something else</a>. Better you find that
			out here than a month in.
		</p>
	</div>

	<div class="border border-ticket-rule bg-cream px-5 py-5 shadow-ticket sm:px-6 lg:rotate-[1.5deg]" data-reveal>
		<p class="font-mono text-eyebrow font-semibold tracking-wide text-amber-deep">
			NOT FOR · {spellCapital(notFor.length).toUpperCase()} KITCHENS
		</p>
		<ul role="list" class="mt-4">
			{
				notFor.map((entry) => (
					<li class="border-t border-dashed border-ticket-rule py-4">
						<p class="font-semibold">{entry.title}</p>
						<p class="mt-1.5 max-w-[52ch] text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">{entry.body}</p>
					</li>
				))
			}
		</ul>
	</div>
	</div>

	<SectionHandoff from="who" />
</section>
